    "domestic_electricity_zero_vat": {
      "description": "VAT on domestic electricity is 0% instead of 5% from 1 October 2026 to 30 June 2027: in Great Britain to March 2027 and across the UK from April 2027. The model's baseline has no zero rate, so the measure covers the whole period, as the Treasury costs it. It applies to electricity spending only. Each year carries its share of a year's electricity use, not a share of its days (DESNZ Energy Trends Table 5.5): 2026-27 the October to March share (about 57%), 2027-28 the April to June share (about 22%).",
